examples_proposed:
Python error handling example: 
try:
    client.chat.send(stream=True)
except RedwoodError as e:
    # e.error_code == "NETWORK_TRANSIENT" or "MODEL_OOM"
    print(e.stable_id, e.short_recovery_hint)
    if e.retriable:
        time.sleep(e.retry_after_seconds or 1)
        client.chat.resume_from(e.resume_token)

TypeScript quick-fix: 
try {
  await client.chat.stream(req)
} catch (e) {
  // e.error_code === 'AUTH_EXPIRED'
  console.log(e.stable_id, e.recovery_hint)
  if (e.retriable) {
    setTimeout(() => client.chat.retry(req), e.retry_after_seconds ?? 1000)
  }
}

Go snippet for idempotent retry: 
resp, err := client.ChatStream(ctx, req)
if err != nil {
  if sdk.IsRetriable(err) {
    // extract stable id and resume token
    time.Sleep(time.Second)
    client.ResumeStream(ctx, err.ResumeToken())
  }
}
